    "result_text": "There's only one test class, and the full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec asked for an `initials` field on the owner \u2014 the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nTwo changes, following the existing `displayName` pattern (a computed, read-only owner field):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema (the source of the generated `OwnerDto`), alongside `displayName`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` that computes it:\n   ```java\n   owner.getFirstName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\" + owner.getLastName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\"\n   ```\n   Both names are `required` with `minLength: 1` in the schema, so `substring(0, 1)` is always safe.\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{ownerId}` pipeline already responds via `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, so no OfficeFloor wiring changes were needed. The `AcceptanceTest` (asserting `\"john\"`/`\"smith\"` \u2192 `J.S.`) and the full suite both pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
